      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This feeling of erasure, like a deleted character in a story, is a profound form of grief that goes beyond simple loss. When the version of you that gave life meaning is gone, the weight of simply existing can feel insurmountable because the underlying reason to continue no longer feels present. It is human to feel that the point has vanished when the core of your identity dissolves, and your exhaustion is valid even if there is no immediate \"fix.\"",
      "source": "target",
